aximum and minimum values. \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}_{\\text{min}}+{y}_{\\text{max}}}{2} & =\\frac{6+10}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{2} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the midline is $y=8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251409 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "933b20c7-323f-5443-9cf4-97e87fa2c6fc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Midline of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6528833d-2b00-5207-b35b-dd0b6e74426a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251411} {:answer/id #uuid "346350ca-04db-5dd1-acfa-eab38938cd51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251412} {:answer/id #uuid "c2f0ad21-20fe-5c09-b69b-b08654f20d0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251413} {:answer/id #uuid "1201b252-ed82-5bb4-8dad-2e7d5f766eec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251414} {:answer/id #uuid "3acb553b-7c22-5ff6-9103-4c02f35f016f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3acb553b-7c22-5ff6-9103-4c02f35f016f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251415} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9caca9e-06c8-588c-be0f-4c6dc7fcef16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251410}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "03945e80-ab7c-5051-baf3-b885218e7cfe" :question/math-academy-id "q-236901" :question/problem "Find the equation of the midline for a transformed cosine function with a minimum value of $3$ and a maximum value of $15.$" :question/worked-solution "A sinusoidal graph's midline (or vertical shift) is the horizontal line that divides it vertically in half. \n\nThe equation of the midline is given by\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{{y}_{\\text{min}}+{y}_{\\text{max}}}{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{\\text{min}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{max}}$ are the minimum and maximum values of the function. The midline equals the average of the maximum and minimum values. \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}_{\\text{min}}+{y}_{\\text{max}}}{2} & =\\frac{3+15}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{2} \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the midline is $y=9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251416 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5696c2d5-4e35-5ed3-a4a2-6fe9b158e461" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e4ae1b7-a50b-56be-97ea-77680311a08f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)\\in [-6,1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251418} {:answer/id #uuid "4c8fdad3-87ca-575d-9e0b-36db07bdecbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)\\in [0,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251419} {:answer/id #uuid "0b0887d8-4d49-5398-8e8a-80bcef76e7c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)\\in [-4,0]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251420} {:answer/id #uuid "454284d9-321e-5280-bc6e-49d5274c870f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)\\in [-1,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251421} {:answer/id #uuid "a9871169-55b5-5d4f-8109-b991e0877f51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)\\in [-3,3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251422}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "454284d9-321e-5280-bc6e-49d5274c870f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)\\in [-1,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251421} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4c3aebc-e240-5449-8dd6-b3ffdecdd60d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251417}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dce67c89-e05b-50af-a500-c7c6cd8191cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-40903" :question/problem "What is the range of $f(x)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})+2?$" :question/worked-solution "The range of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\le 1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $3$ and then adding $2$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\le 1 \\\\  & -3\\le 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\le 3 \\\\  & -1\\le 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})+2\\le 5 \\\\  & -1\\le f(x)\\le 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $f(x)\\in [-1,5].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251423 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5696c2d5-4e35-5ed3-a4a2-6fe9b158e461" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "376948c7-3e1d-554c-bc02-dd4348cb21ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [-2,6]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251425} {:answer/id #uuid "f9083a03-aa14-59d2-b42d-a7598bc1a6df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [2,6]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251426} {:answer/id #uuid "fe54b646-c22a-5d08-aa8b-730b7b388416" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [3,6]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251427} {:answer/id #uuid "7b34a9ba-01bb-5baa-9892-a0aa1f80fd4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [4,6]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251428} {:answer/id #uuid "2a47dc30-f61a-5b22-9ed7-0d9d04d69b71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [2,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251429}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9083a03-aa14-59d2-b42d-a7598bc1a6df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [2,6]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251426} :answer-field/id #uuid "35778d9a-65e5-5c71-aa1d-63da9e9c8a5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251424}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5bd0aeca-39f2-5ae1-bf53-35a78055e053" :question/math-academy-id "q-41840" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $y=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{30}^{∘})+4?$" :question/worked-solution "The range of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{30}^{∘})\\le 1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-2$ and then adding $4$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{30}^{∘})\\le 1 \\\\ 2 & \\ge -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{30}^{∘})\\ge -2 \\\\ 6 & \\ge -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{30}^{∘})+4\\ge 2 \\\\ 2 & \\le y\\le 6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $y\\in [2,6].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251430 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5696c2d5-4e35-5ed3-a4a2-6fe9b158e461" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc9efe75-c138-5da2-b848-193bb72c340b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [-3,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251432} {:answer/id #uuid "4102e8e0-a690-597a-a997-10821b022901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [-5,3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251433} {:answer/id #uuid "89240193-bff3-550f-8f18-38ffb55d45e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [-1,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251434} {:answer/id #uuid "d952c761-f6bd-5712-8563-2a9172fce59b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [0,2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251435} {:answer/id #uuid "da497e75-85f8-505e-8fe2-251f9c3f3b6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [-5,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251436}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc9efe75-c138-5da2-b848-193bb72c340b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [-3,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251432} :answer-field/id #uuid "26efb4c6-4d6d-5ee0-9f9d-41b8f066281d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251431}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "668aa8db-976b-5e49-9fda-839d6015d588" :question/math-academy-id "q-41964" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $y=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{30}^{∘})+1?$" :question/worked-solution "The range of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{30}^{∘})\\le 1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-4$ and then adding $1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{30}^{∘})\\le 1 \\\\  & 4\\ge -4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{30}^{∘})\\ge -4 \\\\  & 5\\ge -4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{30}^{∘})+1\\ge -3 \\\\  & -3\\le y\\le 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $y\\in [-3,5].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129719 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1eeb42af-74ee-53d7-af9f-be171f77968f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Period of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87c37d2c-edba-5b87-9d3c-6d623636424a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128109} {:answer/id #uuid "ab8b3a78-f3ef-5c40-a8ad-25bfd0c68568" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128110} {:answer/id #uuid "be60d53d-5494-582f-b6f5-c750c14d0b96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128111} {:answer/id #uuid "e3568e22-3bb2-5a35-b158-b9cc3ea9db9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128112} {:answer/id #uuid "f14830ee-654f-5683-b84d-63b482a6a7e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128113}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87c37d2c-edba-5b87-9d3c-6d623636424a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128109} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbca2832-2a18-51fa-aac1-c3efe3977276" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128108}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4126b1b4-8e8d-506d-b0ce-d7e1e1256bf6" :question/math-academy-id "q-43404" :question/problem "Calculate the period of the function $f(x) = \\frac{1}{6}\\sin (\\frac{5x}{3} - \\frac{\\pi }{2})$." :question/worked-solution "Given a function in the form $f(x)=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the period $T$ is given by $\\frac{2\\pi }{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=\\frac{5}{3}.$ Therefore, the period is $\\frac{2\\pi }{(\\frac{5}{3})}=\\frac{6\\pi }{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251437 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1eeb42af-74ee-53d7-af9f-be171f77968f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Period of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dfdb7d62-1815-5d29-acfe-622febb28f10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251439} {:answer/id #uuid "5014926f-7f59-5b3d-8517-bc6f06c7ec42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251440} {:answer/id #uuid "5ca60e71-2205-50ab-83b7-f4e577cf0e61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{15}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251441} {:answer/id #uuid "2f64cdad-6aa8-5b2a-b04d-9ad004a9719e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251442} {:answer/id #uuid "e8bfa896-64ab-5c41-88b9-f47573d376e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{75}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5014926f-7f59-5b3d-8517-bc6f06c7ec42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251440} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bbdef70-c3e6-539e-a2a7-0627d5fd6505" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251438}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fc27469a-2932-515c-94df-5bd78adb639c" :question/math-academy-id "q-43411" :question/problem "What is the period of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x+{90}^{∘})?$" :question/worked-solution "Given a function in the form $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the period is ${360}^{∘}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=8.$ Therefore, the period is $\\frac{{360}^{∘}}{8}={45}^{∘}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251444 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f8fa2b3-ccaa-5390-89fa-03e338cf8690" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Amplitude of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5985b1d0-fe39-5ecb-9fa3-b4f30ea8bef3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251446} {:answer/id #uuid "e496ae29-a38c-5375-b7f1-3288141efc2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251447} {:answer/id #uuid "02b1b0a1-b6aa-5bda-81d8-9fd049cb817e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251448} {:answer/id #uuid "557cc16d-195e-5a1e-9205-2f4c75c7f41d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251449} {:answer/id #uuid "9b935b6c-07ba-55c4-9fd9-2ddb90ba1b69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251450}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "557cc16d-195e-5a1e-9205-2f4c75c7f41d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251449} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb31663a-2380-589f-8a83-19173b75c475" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251445}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3a15f3af-68d8-5a8c-b8e0-62ef440c908d" :question/math-academy-id "q-53428" :question/problem "What is the amplitude of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{3})?$" :question/worked-solution "Given a function in the form $f(x)=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the amplitude is $|A|.$ \n\nSince $A=1,$ we have that the amplitude is $|A|=|1|=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251451 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5696c2d5-4e35-5ed3-a4a2-6fe9b158e461" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da6117df-0691-59d4-81d0-ff90a294b6c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251453} {:answer/id #uuid "cc517720-6a78-52d5-88c8-d36de7a0459a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251454} {:answer/id #uuid "6feb74ed-36af-50e7-89a5-c2f790dbf53e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251455} {:answer/id #uuid "4760d23d-612d-5dea-b2b9-c29691f3e317" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251456} {:answer/id #uuid "bbcfdb62-d630-59f9-8159-dcbe6be9b329" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da6117df-0691-59d4-81d0-ff90a294b6c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251453} :answer-field/id #uuid "840d7e53-e0ee-5a34-93b8-df7c479b2fe0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251452}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7a29f414-ae50-540f-8870-df0e5066e0bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-65928" :question/problem "What is the minimum value of $f(x)=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+\\pi )-4?$" :question/worked-solution "The range of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+\\pi )\\le 1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-1$ and then subtracting $4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+\\pi )\\le 1 \\\\ 1 & \\ge -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+\\pi )\\ge -1 \\\\ -3 & \\ge -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+\\pi )-4\\ge -5 \\\\ -5 & \\le f(x)\\le -3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value is $-5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251458 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1eeb42af-74ee-53d7-af9f-be171f77968f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Period of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e247db7-daab-5c77-8799-b46234a24ac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251460} {:answer/id #uuid "9ec37af6-7563-585c-be67-3905e6f8c039" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{40}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251461} {:answer/id #uuid "db54ffda-9247-5548-ae7d-37c6e33d2ad7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251462} {:answer/id #uuid "e989487d-00f1-5de4-8bdb-f502669aae65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{75}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251463} {:answer/id #uuid "83030191-6cd2-5c6e-8820-07111fa524b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ec37af6-7563-585c-be67-3905e6f8c039" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{40}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251461} :answer-field/id #uuid "525393e2-788c-5d0f-bf3e-a3851889bf52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251459}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2e321d6f-c7e7-53ba-891f-3b32cbcdbc30" :question/math-academy-id "q-81513" :question/problem "What is the period of the function $f(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x-{1}^{∘})?$" :question/worked-solution "Given a function in the form $f(x)=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the period is $\\frac{{360}^{∘}}{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=9.$ Therefore, the period is $\\frac{{360}^{∘}}{9}={40}^{∘}.$"}]}
